course: dictionary
lesson: 13325
title: A dip called guacamole
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You may meet a word you do not know on a menu, in a recipe or at a party. The words around it leave clues. «We ate tortilla chips with a bowl of guacamole.» You dip chips into something, so guacamole must be a food you dip with.
explain: «Mum mashed two ripe avocados, then added lime and chopped tomato to make guacamole.» Mashed means squashed until soft, so the clues show that guacamole is made from avocado. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Guac is a short, informal name for guacamole, and friends often say it when they are chatting. When you are unsure, check a dictionary. It will tell you that guacamole is a green dip or sauce from Mexico.
fact: Guacamole is a green dip or sauce from Mexico.
fact: It is made by mashing avocado, usually with lime, onion, tomato, chilli and salt.
fact: Guacamole is uncountable, so we say «some guacamole», not «a guacamole» or «guacamoles».
fact: Guac is an informal, short name for guacamole.
fact: Guacamole is often eaten with tortilla chips.
exercise: «We dipped the tortilla chips into the bowl of guacamole.» What is guacamole? | A hot pudding served with custard | A kind of bread roll | *A green dip made from avocado | A loud party game
exercise: Which ingredient is usually found in guacamole? | Sugar | Melted chocolate | *Lime | Cream
exercise: «The cook mashed the avocado for the guacamole.» Find and copy the word that means squashed until soft. | *mashed | cook | avocado | guacamole
test: What is guacamole mostly made from? | Mashed potato | Fresh orange juice | Melted cheese | *Mashed avocado
test: Which word is the informal, short name for guacamole? | guava | *guac | guacamo | gecko
exam: Sam reads «She made a bowl of guacamole with lime, onion and chilli.» What does guacamole mean? | A type of trainer | *A green dip or sauce made from mashed avocado | A sweet cake with cream on top | A hot drink served at breakfast
